{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 370,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Thank you to Draper and its Hack the Moon\ninitiative for supporting PBS Digital Studios."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 5410,
    "dDurationMs": 3550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For much of human history, people believed\nthat the planet Earth was the center"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 8960,
    "dDurationMs": 1200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the universe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 10160,
    "dDurationMs": 1030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's understandable."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 11190,
    "dDurationMs": 2020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Earth is pretty big."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 13210,
    "dDurationMs": 3330,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We now know that it's a speck compared to\nthe Universe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 16540,
    "dDurationMs": 5260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To get a sense of that scale, consider this\ngrain of sand held at arm’s length."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 21800,
    "dDurationMs": 4190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In that tiny area covered there are almost\n10,000 entire galaxies."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 25990,
    "dDurationMs": 4520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That’s a quadrillion stars, and as many\nplanetary systems."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 30510,
    "dDurationMs": 5160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In fact there are surely more entire worlds\nin the observable universe than there are"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 35670,
    "dDurationMs": 1630,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "grains of sand on this one."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 43380,
    "dDurationMs": 6020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Less than a century ago we didn’t know that\na universe existed beyond our own Milky Way Galaxy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 49520,
    "dDurationMs": 4600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In the last hundred years our perspective\nand our understanding has grown enormously"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 54129,
    "dDurationMs": 7020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "– to include countless galaxies to the cosmic\nhorizon and almost to the beginning of time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 61149,
    "dDurationMs": 4651,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But before we could map the universe, first\nwe had to discover the universe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 65800,
    "dDurationMs": 4660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We’re at the Mt. Wilson Observatory on the\noutskirts of Los Angeles, California.This"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 70460,
    "dDurationMs": 6150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is where Edwin Hubble made a paradigm-shifting\ndiscovery: in 1924 he proved that the universe"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 76610,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "exists beyond the Milky Way."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 79130,
    "dDurationMs": 2030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Oh my god."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 81160,
    "dDurationMs": 7480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is the Hooker Telescope at Mt. Wilson\nObservatory. It is beautiful."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 88640,
    "dDurationMs": 8610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The whole dome is built of Carnegie Iron in\nthe years when most of the iron was being"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 97250,
    "dDurationMs": 2410,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "sent to the front for tanks."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 99660,
    "dDurationMs": 1400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This thing was built in 1914."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 101060,
    "dDurationMs": 5140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That’s not to say we’d never seen other\ngalaxies – Andromeda is visible to the naked"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 106200,
    "dDurationMs": 2370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "eye – if you have good vision."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 108570,
    "dDurationMs": 5130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And many nearby galaxies were visible as fuzzy\nblobs in our early telescopes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 113700,
    "dDurationMs": 4140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But as far as we knew they were just clouds\nof gas inside our own galaxy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 117840,
    "dDurationMs": 5370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The philosopher Immanual Kant guessed that\ntheses nebulae might be entire “island universes”,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 123220,
    "dDurationMs": 1980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of their own."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 125200,
    "dDurationMs": 6899,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In 1915, the American astronomer Vesto Slipher\nreported that some of those fuzzy blobs were"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 132100,
    "dDurationMs": 6420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "zipping away from us so quickly that they\nwould surely escape the Milky Way’s gravitational field."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 138520,
    "dDurationMs": 5579,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It was a clue that they were, in fact, never\nwithin the Milky Way in the first place."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 144099,
    "dDurationMs": 6461,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But to prove that these spiral nebulae were\nreally island universes, we needed to find"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 150560,
    "dDurationMs": 1289,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "their distances."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 151849,
    "dDurationMs": 4051,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And distance is one of the hardest things\nto measure in astronomy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 155900,
    "dDurationMs": 5309,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So that's the desk and chair where Edwin Hubble\nconducted his observations of Andromeda to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 161209,
    "dDurationMs": 1481,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "calculate its distance."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 162690,
    "dDurationMs": 6820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He would spend nights up there taking photographs,\nsensitive photographic plates using a camera"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 169510,
    "dDurationMs": 2849,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "much like this one."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 172359,
    "dDurationMs": 2011,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Photographic plates go right in here."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 174370,
    "dDurationMs": 5349,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "See, when you look through a telescope it\nflattens 3-D space into a two-dimensional"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 179719,
    "dDurationMs": 5561,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "image a dome above our heads that the ancients\ncalled the celestial sphere."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 185280,
    "dDurationMs": 2159,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "All sense of distance is lost."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 187440,
    "dDurationMs": 6580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For example, consider two stars – one bright\none dim to our eyes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 194020,
    "dDurationMs": 4820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, perhaps those stars are identical, and the\nbright one is just closer to us."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 198840,
    "dDurationMs": 5099,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Or perhaps the bright one is truly much more\nluminous – and is at the same distance or even"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 203939,
    "dDurationMs": 1830,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "further away than the dim star."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 205769,
    "dDurationMs": 6310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now there are some clever ways to measure\ndistances to stars within the Milky Way galaxy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 212079,
    "dDurationMs": 1970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But in another galaxy?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 214049,
    "dDurationMs": 5890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Not likely – at least not until the brilliant\nwork of astronomer Henrietta Leavitt."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 219939,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A decade before Hubble made his discovery,\nLeavitt discovered that a certain type of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 224739,
    "dDurationMs": 5041,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "star, Cepheid variables, brightened and dimmed\nwith a repeating period that is mathematically"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 229780,
    "dDurationMs": 3179,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "related to the stars’ absolute brightness."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 232959,
    "dDurationMs": 3310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They were the first “standard candles.”"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 236269,
    "dDurationMs": 5900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you time how many days or weeks it took\na given Cepheid to fluctuate and you can determine"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 242169,
    "dDurationMs": 1641,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "its true brightness."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 243810,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So you can also figure out how far away it\nis just by seeing how much its true brightness"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 248810,
    "dDurationMs": 3239,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "has been dimmed by that distance."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 252049,
    "dDurationMs": 5261,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That means if you spot a Cepheid variable\nin a distant spiral nebulae you can find the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 257310,
    "dDurationMs": 1310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "distance to both."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 258620,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And that’s exactly what Hubble did right\nhere."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 262540,
    "dDurationMs": 4980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He looked for Cepheid variables in the Great\nAndromeda Nebula – as it was known back then."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 267520,
    "dDurationMs": 4660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He found that Andromeda is around 2 million light\nyears away."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 272180,
    "dDurationMs": 4389,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Or around 20 times the entire diameter\nof the Milky Way disc."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 276569,
    "dDurationMs": 5441,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The Andromeda Nebula became the Andromeda\ngalaxy and with more distance measurements"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 282010,
    "dDurationMs": 5930,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it became clear that all spiral nebulae were\nisland universes of their own."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 287940,
    "dDurationMs": 2099,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Of course Hubble didn’t stop there."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 290039,
    "dDurationMs": 5880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He combined his distances with Vesto Slipher’s\nvelocities to discover that the galaxies all"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 295919,
    "dDurationMs": 5101,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "appear to be racing away from the Milky Way\n– paving the way for the discovery that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 301020,
    "dDurationMs": 6810,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the universe is expanding, meaning it must\nonce have started with the Big Bang."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 307830,
    "dDurationMs": 4360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "With this telescope, Edwin Hubble not only\ndiscovered the universe beyond the Milky Way,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 312190,
    "dDurationMs": 3979,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but he opened the door to discovering its\nvery origin."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 316169,
    "dDurationMs": 4671,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And to our exploration of the true vastness\nof the universe that followed."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 320840,
    "dDurationMs": 5400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To see where nearly 100 years of exploration\nhas led us, we'll need a little help from"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 326240,
    "dDurationMs": 6600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the Digital Universe built by the Hayden Planetarium\nat the American Museum of Natural History."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 335600,
    "dDurationMs": 1620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We're on our way up."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 337220,
    "dDurationMs": 3150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is where it all happens."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 340370,
    "dDurationMs": 1579,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What a view."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 341949,
    "dDurationMs": 3931,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We're looking down at the Planetarium from\nthe astrophysics department."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 345880,
    "dDurationMs": 5219,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "FYI this is pretty much my favorite place\nin the world and I spend as much time here"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 351099,
    "dDurationMs": 1201,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as I can."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 352300,
    "dDurationMs": 7609,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Folk here at the Hayden have turned that dome\ninto a spaceship. It can fly us through a virtual universe"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 359909,
    "dDurationMs": 4760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "built from the most complete 3D atlas of our\nUniverse ever compiled."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 364669,
    "dDurationMs": 4641,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And unlike regular spaceships, this dome can\nfly at many times the speed of light."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 369310,
    "dDurationMs": 5720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It’s the perfect place to explore the scale\nof the vast universe that Edwin Hubble unlocked"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 375030,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for us."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 376030,
    "dDurationMs": 1500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Let’s take a journey."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 377530,
    "dDurationMs": 4950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We’re now flying through the American Museum\nof Natural History’s Digital Universe, rendered"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 382480,
    "dDurationMs": 1439,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by the OpenSpace Software."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 383919,
    "dDurationMs": 5041,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Leaving Earth, the Sun, and our solar system\nbehind, we’re zipping past the hundreds"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 388960,
    "dDurationMs": 5820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of billions of stars of our Milky Way galaxy\nat a few hundred billion times the speed of light."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 394800,
    "dDurationMs": 5180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "While we’ve only mapped the locations and\nvelocities of around 1% of those stars, that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 399980,
    "dDurationMs": 5469,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "gives us an incredible understanding of the\nshape and motion of our home galaxy – once"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 405449,
    "dDurationMs": 5270,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "imagined to be the entire universe and now\nour very familiar island home."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 410719,
    "dDurationMs": 5061,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As we zoom out, now at several trillion times\nthe speed of light, our local group of galaxies"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 415780,
    "dDurationMs": 1660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "comes into view."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 417440,
    "dDurationMs": 4620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There’s Andromeda, its incredible distance\nfirst revealed to Hubble through its pulsing"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 422060,
    "dDurationMs": 1789,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Cepheid variable stars."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 423849,
    "dDurationMs": 6351,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That’s the Virgo cluster – the nearest\nbig city, of which our local group is an outlying suburb."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 430280,
    "dDurationMs": 5400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Every dot we see is a known galaxy, it’s\nposition, velocity, and even stellar content"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 435689,
    "dDurationMs": 2450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "measured and cataloged."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 438139,
    "dDurationMs": 6310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The latest studies of galaxy motion reveal\nthat Virgo, the Milky Way, and a hundred thousand"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 444449,
    "dDurationMs": 7180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "more galaxies belong Laniakea, a cluster of\nsuperclusters some 500 million light years"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 451629,
    "dDurationMs": 1010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "across."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 452639,
    "dDurationMs": 5250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As we accelerate to one hundred quadrillion\ntimes the speed of light we see the extent"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 457889,
    "dDurationMs": 6981,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of our modern mapping of the universe – galaxies\nassembled into many vast filaments, flowing"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 464870,
    "dDurationMs": 5650,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "together on rivers of dark matter to form\nthe cosmic web, of which Laniakea is just"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 470520,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a part."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 471520,
    "dDurationMs": 3079,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Edwin Hubble never imagined such a structure."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 474599,
    "dDurationMs": 3951,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Those smaller dots at the edge of our surveys\nare quasars."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 478550,
    "dDurationMs": 5880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They look small from here, but each is a maelstrom\nof gas falling into a giant black hole, and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 484430,
    "dDurationMs": 2769,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "each shines out from the core of its own galaxy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 487199,
    "dDurationMs": 3740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That distant light comes to us from a much\nyounger universe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 490939,
    "dDurationMs": 5181,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And so we just flew through an atlas of the some\nof the first galaxies to ever form."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 496120,
    "dDurationMs": 5729,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To see these most distant quasars, as well\nas the earliest galaxies or even black holes"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 501849,
    "dDurationMs": 5651,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or worlds around other stars, Mt. Wilson's\nHooker Telescope wouldn't cut it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 507580,
    "dDurationMs": 6500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For that we need state of the art modern observatories\nlike the Gemini Observatory, and the Event"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 514089,
    "dDurationMs": 3861,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Horizon Telescope, and LIGO, which we visited\nthroughout this series."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 517950,
    "dDurationMs": 4990,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yet it was Edwin Hubble’s observations that\nopened the door to our current appreciation"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 522940,
    "dDurationMs": 3089,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the immensity of our universe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 526029,
    "dDurationMs": 4191,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Knowledge that is revealed here at the Hayden\nPlanetarium."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 530220,
    "dDurationMs": 5260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And hopefully our modern perspective will\nin turn be a gateway to future knowledge."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 535480,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If we continue exploring – if we keep looking\ndeeper and further – who knows what we’ll"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 541000,
    "dDurationMs": 3640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "find in the expanding horizons of space\ntime?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 551680,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Thank you to Draper and its Hack the Moon initiative for supporting PBS Digital Studios."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 556480,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You know the story of the Astronauts who landed on the Moon."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 559760,
    "dDurationMs": 7920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, you can visit wehackthemoon.com and discover the story of the male and female engineers who guided them there and back safely."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 567680,
    "dDurationMs": 5480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Hack the Moon chronicles the engineers and technologies behind the Apollo missions."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 573160,
    "dDurationMs": 6120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Brought to you by Draper, the site is full of images, videos and stories about the people who hacked the moon"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 579280,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If the size of the Universe is enormous, why\nhaven’t we seen other signs of life?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 584000,
    "dDurationMs": 7360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you want answer to that, head over to It’s\nOkay to Be Smart to watch Joe Hanson explore"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 591520,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "how to calculate the possibility that advanced\nalien civilizations are out there."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 595920,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "PBS is bringing you the universe with the\nSUMMER OF SPACE, which includes six incredible"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 601200,
    "dDurationMs": 6480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "new science and history shows airing on PBS\nand streaming on PBS.org and the PBS Video app."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 607680,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Watch it all on PBS.org/summerofspace."
    } ]
  } ]
}
